From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 13:28:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: dump SRNG stats before recovery teardown

QMI FW_READY events are processed on a workqueue separate from
restart_work. A repeated event can read the old ring pointers while
restart_work frees and replaces their coherent DMA storage.

Dump the old rings from restart_work before it tears them down.
Invalidate their initialized state when the HAL is dismantled, so a
later restart also skips rings that were not set up again.

Link: https://github.com/VIKINGYFY/immortalwrt/issues/236

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
@@ -1474,6 +1474,11 @@
 	if (test_bit(ATH12K_GROUP_FLAG_DS_QUARANTINED, &ab->ag->flags))
 		return -EIO;
 	mutex_lock(&ab->core_lock);
+
+	/* The old rings still have their DMA storage on this workqueue. */
+	if (ab->is_reset)
+		ath12k_hal_dump_srng_stats(ab);
+
 	ath12k_link_sta_rhash_tbl_destroy(ab);
 	ath12k_thermal_unregister(ab);
 	ath12k_dp_pdev_free(ab);
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/hal.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/hal.c
@@ -765,6 +765,10 @@
 void ath12k_hal_srng_deinit(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 {
 	struct ath12k_hal *hal = &ab->hal;
+	int ring_id;
+
+	for (ring_id = 0; ring_id < HAL_SRNG_RING_ID_MAX; ring_id++)
+		hal->srng_list[ring_id].initialized = 0;
 
 	ath12k_hal_unregister_srng_lock_keys(hal);
 	ath12k_hal_free_cont_rdp(hal);
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
@@ -4446,9 +4446,6 @@
 
 			clear_bit(ATH12K_FLAG_QMI_FAIL, &ab->dev_flags);
 			if (test_bit(ATH12K_FLAG_QMI_FW_READY_COMPLETE, &ab->dev_flags)) {
-				if (ab->is_reset)
-					ath12k_hal_dump_srng_stats(ab);
-
 				set_bit(ATH12K_FLAG_RECOVERY, &ab->dev_flags);
 				queue_work(ab->workqueue, &ab->restart_work);
 				break;
